# Architecture document — read and maintain

[`ARCHITECTURE.md`](../../ARCHITECTURE.md) is the canonical map of Visita. Agents must treat it as source of truth alongside the code.

## Before starting work

1. **Read** `ARCHITECTURE.md` (at least the sections relevant to your task: packages, APIs, data model, checklist).
2. Skim existing code in the same package — match naming and layering already documented there.

## While implementing

- Follow layering and naming in ARCHITECTURE.md §7–§9 and [visita-layered-architecture.mdc](visita-layered-architecture.mdc).
- New routes, tables, packages, auth rules, or client tracking behavior → plan an ARCHITECTURE.md update in the same change.

## Before marking a task done

Update `ARCHITECTURE.md` when you changed any of:

| Change | Update |
|--------|--------|
| New or renamed REST path | §4–§6 API tables |
| New entity / table / migration | §3, §11 |
| New package or moved class | §8 package layout |
| New auth or filter | §2 lifecycle, §10 |
| New dev seed expectations | §13 + [development-experience.mdc](development-experience.mdc) |
| New test convention | §7 Testing |
| New config property | §14 |

Keep edits **concise** — tables and bullet lists, not prose essays. Remove or fix stale entries in the same PR.

## Never

- Add significant behavior without checking ARCHITECTURE.md first.
- Leave ARCHITECTURE.md out of date after a structural change.
- Duplicate long architecture prose in rules or comments — link to `ARCHITECTURE.md` instead.
